---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CapabilityPlate from "../../components/CapabilityPlate.astro";
import { loadAtlasExperience } from "../../lib/atlas";

const { capabilities } = loadAtlasExperience();
const classLabel = {
  secret: "Secret key material",
  watch: "Public derivation",
  public: "Public destination",
  variable: "Context dependent",
  coordination: "Coordination data",
  proof: "Bound proof",
};
---
<Base title="What am I holding? · BIP Atlas" description="A capability atlas for wallet artifacts: what each one can do, what it cannot establish, and what sharing it can reveal." current="capabilities">
  <div class="manual-page atlas-flow capability-intro">
    <p class="atlas-specimen">FIELD NOTE · C01</p>
    <h1>What am I holding?</h1>
    <p class="atlas-dek">A mnemonic, an xpub, a descriptor, an address and a PSBT can all look like wallet strings. Their capability boundaries are very different.</p>
    <p>
      This atlas compares what each artifact is made for, what it can do, what it cannot establish and what sharing it can reveal.
      It is a conceptual guide, not a classifier. Never paste real wallet material into a website to identify it.
    </p>
    <aside class="capability-caveat" aria-label="Important scope limits">
      <span>READ THE BOUNDARY, NOT JUST THE LABEL</span>
      <p>Descriptors may contain private keys. PSBTs vary in completeness and contents; a final signed transaction is not an unsigned PSBT. A valid encoding never proves ownership or safety.</p>
    </aside>
    <nav class="capability-index" aria-label="Artifact index">
      <p class="capability-index__label">THE SPECIMEN INDEX</p>
      <ol>
        {capabilities.artifacts.map((artifact, index) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`#${artifact.id}`} data-classification={artifact.classification}>
              <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
              <strong>{artifact.label}</strong>
              <small>{classLabel[artifact.classification]}</small>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </nav>
  </div>

  <div class="manual-page capability-atlas">
    {capabilities.artifacts.map((artifact, index) => <CapabilityPlate artifact={artifact} index={index} />)}
  </div>

  <div class="manual-page atlas-flow capability-outro">
    <h2>Keep the distinctions</h2>
    <p>Validity is not ownership. Public derivation is not zero privacy cost. A signing package is not a payment. A proof is not an identity.</p>
    <p class="atlas-small">Every plate above leads into the chapter sections that carry the full explanation and its evidence. For relationships between mechanisms, open the <a href="/map/">relationship atlas</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
